                          Installing Lunar Conquest

                                   V2.00+

                                  22/10/96

This installation assumes that you are:
                                       Using the CNet BBS program
                                       Familiar with the Amiga
                                       Not braindead.

Step 1:  UnLHA the archive.  (since you're reading this, you've probably
         already done that.)

         Unregistered File List
         ------------------------------------------------------------------
         File               Size  Description
         ------------------------------------------------------------------
         LCu               338264 Main File
         LC-Maintenance     76584 Nightly Maintenance
         ComEspDoc.txt       3672 Help File
         Galactic.txt        1811 Help File
         Hints.txt           1114 Help File
         LunarConquest.txt   6668 Help File
         NewUserDocs.txt     1520 Help File
         SysOpDocs.txt       1938 Help File
         Install.readme      4436 Installation Instructions
         Register.readme     2893 Registering Instructions
         ------------------------------------------------------------------

         Registered File List
         ------------------------------------------------------------------
         File               Size  Description
         ------------------------------------------------------------------
         LC                337676 Main File
         LC-Maintenance     76584 Nightly Maintenance
         LC-SetUp           86776 Default Set Up and SysOp Password Maker
         LC-SetUp.info       2038 Icon
         ComEspDoc.txt       3672 Help File
         Galactic.txt        1811 Help File
         Hints.txt           1114 Help File
         LunarConquest.txt   6668 Help File
         NewUserDocs.txt     1520 Help File
         SysOpDocs.txt       1938 Help File
         Install.readme      4436 Installation Instructions
         Register.readme     2893 Registering Instructions
         ------------------------------------------------------------------

         If any of the .txt files are missing, don't worry - the program
         won't crash without them.  If the main file or the maintenance
         file is missing, you have a problem.

Step 2:  Put the files in the right place.  You should copy the ENTIRE
         LunarConquest directory into your `PFiles:' directory.  You can
         put the LC-SetUp program somewhere else if you want since you will
         be running it from Workbench anyway.

Step 3:  Make the assign.  Add a line to your User-Startup as follows:
         Assign LunarConquest: PFiles:LunarConquest/
         Now, either reboot your Amiga or use `Execute Command' from the
         Workbench and enter the same assign as you put in your
         User-Startup.  It is very important that you do this BEFORE
         running any of the Lunar Conquest files.

If you have the unregistered version, you can't set any of the defaults or
set the SysOp Password.  You won't be able to use the SysOp functions.  You
can skip right to Step 5.

Step 4:  Go to Workbench and double click on the LC-SetUp icon.  It will
         open a screen with all the alterable settings on it.  If you move
         the mouse to the bottom of the screen, the page will scroll up.
         Moving the mouse to the top of the screen will scroll the page
         down.  Clicking the left mouse button on an item will allow you to
         change that item.  If nothing else, set the SysOp Password (bottom
         entry).  If you don't, you won't be able to access the Sysop Menu.
         Clicking the right mouse button in the title section will quit the
         program without saving.  Clicking the left mouse button will save
         the .DFT file and the .PWD file.

Step 5:  Log on to your BBS.  Go to your PFiles section.  Enter `A'.  When
         prompted, enter `D' for a DOS program.  Enter `LunarConquest:LC'
         (`LunarConquest:LCu' for the unregistered version) as the program
         name.  Enter `Lunar Conquest V2.00 by FBN' for the program
         description.  Enter `%1 %7' as the arguments.  Disable More Mode.
         Allow only one user at a time.  Save the entry.

Congratulations!  You've completed the installation procedure for Lunar
Conquest V2.00+.  Now, log on to your BBS and play.
